{
  "about": "E6 S2: the adapted copy of dew_flow_mcp tests/Mcp.Tests/Leftovers at 21553ce (plan D2), plus DirectoryLinks.cs and RepositoryRoot.cs. Per file: upstream path, target path, upstream git blob SHA, ordered exact-replace operations with their match counts and, beyond the namespace line, a reason. TheAdaptedCopyTests undoes them in reverse on the raw bytes, compares the git blob SHA, and applies them forward again. Limits (plan D3): F29 is closed by copy - on Windows the sweep holds coai's per-root named mutex (SweepLock.cs, benchmark's own file) over its whole pass, so two sweeps of one temp root never interleave. F31 - on Windows, what a run leaves in a process whose NEW files and folders are owned by BUILTIN\\Administrators (measured: pwsh on windows-latest) is not removed by the sweep and not named by the audit; it waits for a person. An elevated Git Bash makes the caller's files (measured), and the limit does not apply there.",
